`hexQ m` lists the 34 coordinates (`x₀, y₀, x₁, y₁, …`) of the core `hexLU m` (`N18Core.lean`) as elements of
`ℚ(√3) ⊆ ℚ(√2, √3)`: the hexagon `2 e^{i 60° i}`, the centre, and ten of the twelve boundary points
`ρ₁₉ e^{i (15° + 30° j)}` (`ρ₁₉ e^{i 15°} = (2 + √3) + i`).
-/

